.TH "OCONSOLE" "1" "" "Onesimus 25.1.2+onesimus.0.2.0" "Onesimus"
.SH NAME
oconsole \- console of the Onesimus and Bareos Directors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oconsole
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B oconsole
.RI [ options ]
.B \-e
.I command
.br
.B oconsole \-\-mcp
.RB [ \-\-mcp\-http
.IR address ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B oconsole
connects to a Director and sends console commands, like
.BR bconsole (1).
It speaks gRPC to the Onesimus Director (tried first) and the classic
Bareos console protocol (BNET) to every Director, including bareos\-dir.
The interactive mode offers completion, fish\-style suggestions and key
bindings built from the Director's command grammar.
.PP
With
.B \-\-mcp
it serves the Model Context Protocol for AI assistants instead: on
stdin/stdout, or as Streamable HTTP with
.BR \-\-mcp\-http .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " path" "\fR, \fP\-\-config " path
Configuration file. Default: /etc/bareos/oconsole.conf, then
/etc/bareos/bconsole.conf.
.TP
.BI \-a " address" "\fR, \fP\-\-address " address
Director address (overrides the configuration).
.TP
.BI \-p " port" "\fR, \fP\-\-port " port
Director port (overrides the configuration).
.TP
.BI \-n " name" "\fR, \fP\-\-name " name
Console name (overrides the configuration).
.TP
.BI \-w " password" "\fR, \fP\-\-password " password
Password (overrides the configuration).
.TP
.B \-\-grpc
Use gRPC only, without falling back to BNET.
.TP
.B \-\-bnet
Use the classic console protocol (BNET) only.
.TP
.BI \-\-grpc\-port " port"
gRPC port. Default: Director port + 1000.
.TP
.BI \-\-grpc\-fingerprint " sha256"
Expected SHA\-256 fingerprint of the Director's gRPC certificate.
Default: ~/.config/oconsole/known_directors, asked on first use.
.TP
.BI \-e " command" "\fR, \fP\-\-command " command
Run one command, print its reply and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-mcp
Serve the Model Context Protocol on stdin/stdout.
.TP
.BI \-\-mcp\-http " address"
Serve MCP as Streamable HTTP at /mcp on this address (read only unless the
development build allows writing).
.TP
.BI \-\-mcp\-token\-file " path"
Bearer token file for \-\-mcp\-http (created with mode 0600 if missing).
.TP
.BI \-\-mcp\-host " authority"
Additional HTTP Host authority to accept (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-mcp\-read\-only
Offer only the read tools, also on stdio.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fP\-\-help
Print the options.
.TP
.B \-V\fR, \fP\-\-version
Print the version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
The configuration file has the bconsole syntax: a
.B Director
resource (Name, Address, Port, Password) and optionally a
.B Console
resource (Name, Password) for a named console. The MCP mode logs in as the
console whose name ends in
.BR \-mcp ,
if there is one.
.SH PROMPT
.PP
The interactive prompt has the form
.PP
.RS
.IB console @ director [ version ]>
.RE
.PP
.I console
is the name of the
.B Console
resource
.B oconsole
logs in with: the
.B Name
of the Console resource in the configuration file. The Director knows a
console of that name and applies its ACLs and profiles to every command.
Without a Console resource
.B oconsole
logs in as the Director's default console and the prompt shows
.BR *UserAgent* .
.I director
is the name the Director reports (over gRPC in the session reply, over BNET
in the banner
.BR "1000 OK: \fIname\fP Version: ..." ),
.I version
the version of
.BR oconsole .
For example, with
.B "Console { Name = \(dqoconsole\(dq }"
in the configuration file, against a Director named
.B bareos\-dir
(the Bareos default):
.PP
.RS
.BI oconsole@bareos\-dir[ version ]>
.RE
.PP
On a terminal the prompt is green while a command may be sent and red
during the three seconds the rate guard keeps after each command.
.SH COMPLETION
.PP
At connect
.B oconsole
loads the command grammar with
.BR ".api 2" ,
.B .grammar
and
.BR ".api 0" ,
and again after
.B reload
and
.BR configure .
The grammar lists only the commands the console may run. A Director
without
.B .grammar
(bareos\-dir, older odir) answers "is an invalid command"; then the
completion is built from
.BR .help .
The values of resource names (clients, jobs, pools, volumes, ...) are read
once at connect with the dot commands the grammar names.
.PP
.B Tab
completes the word at the cursor: the command, then the subcommand words,
keywords and
.B key=
of the arguments, then values after
.BR key= ,
also after a comma in a list value. Arguments already given are not
offered again unless they are repeatable; once one member of an exclusive
group is given, the others are left out. Required arguments come first.
Values with blanks are quoted.
.PP
While typing, a dimmed suggestion follows the cursor at the end of the line:
the newest history line that starts with the input, else (as in fish) the
rest of the first completion of the word being typed, even among several,
else the usage of the next arguments. Lines the Director refused are not
suggested.
.PP
.B help
.I command
prints the usage, description, arguments and examples from the grammar
(the text of the man page
.BR odir\-\fIcommand\fR (7)).
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Up\fR, \fPDown
As in fish: walk the history backwards or forwards through the lines that
start with the text typed before the first key (all lines on an empty line),
skipping repeats; Down past the newest line brings back the typed text.
.TP
.B Right\fR, \fPCtrl\-F\fR, \fPEnd
At the end of the line with a suggestion: accept the whole suggestion;
otherwise move right or to the end.
.TP
.B Alt\-Right\fR, \fPAlt\-F
With a suggestion: accept its next word; otherwise move one word forward.
.TP
.B Tab
Complete; several candidates are listed.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-R
Incremental history search.
.TP
.B Esc
Hide the suggestion until the line changes.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-C
Clear the line and stay connected; while a command runs, cancel it.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-D
On an empty line: quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/bareos/oconsole.conf
Configuration (fallback /etc/bareos/bconsole.conf).
.TP
.I ~/.oconsole_history
Command history.
.TP
.I ~/.config/oconsole/known_directors
Accepted gRPC certificate fingerprints.
